# Windows build outputs - CLAUDE.md already documented these as
# "gitignored, regenerated not committed", but no actual .gitignore
# entry ever existed for them, so all three had been committed since
# early history: a full Windows venv (.venv-build/, 262MB, 7949 files)
# and two PyInstaller output trees (AVG APP/, dist/, 433MB/1294 files
# each). Removed from this branch's tree (linux-port has no use for any
# of the three - the Linux equivalents are .venv-linux/, already
# ignored above, and this branch doesn't use PyInstaller at all, see
# docs/linux-port/WINDOWS_VS_LINUX.md's "Packaging shape" entry).
# Untouched on main/development, where they're still real build outputs
# even though they were never meant to be committed there either.
.venv-build/
AVG APP/
dist/

# Vendored ffmpeg build - fetched by tools/fetch_ffmpeg.py, not committed
# (100+ MB either platform's build). The Windows build's copy of this
# ignore rule lives in that build's own .gitignore.
vendor/ffmpeg/

# tools/build_flatpak.ps1 scratch/output - flatpak-builder's own build
# cache and the exported repo + .flatpak bundle "Build installer"
# produces. Regenerated, not committed - same reasoning as build/ above.
build-dir/
flatpak-dist/
.flatpak-builder/
